{"data": [{"author_id": "1968598802237136896", "created_at": "2026-11-10T22:47:31.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2120287263481626981"], "id": "2120287263481626981", "in_reply_to_user_id": "1745106082790318080", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 6, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2120025695283785966", "type": "replied_to"}], "text": "@SemiAnalysis_ Step 6 matters for anyone building the room: HBM5's PHY can draw over 4x HBM4E's power, handled with a thermal chimney on top.\n\nThe memory stack is designing its own cooling. A new thermal budget line, millimetres from the die.\n\nWhere does that heat land in a closed-loop rack?", "url": "https://x.com/Neo_Wake123/status/2120287263481626981"}, {"author_id": "961995849499795456", "created_at": "2026-11-10T21:47:22.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2120272127647715366"], "id": "2120272127647715366", "in_reply_to_user_id": "1745106082790318080", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 1, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2120025695283785966", "type": "replied_to"}], "text": "@SemiAnalysis_ Getting more speed from the same pins is a smart path. I think AI agents will need far more memory than most forecasts assume.", "url": "https://x.com/boundlessanurag/status/2120272127647715366"}, {"author_id": "1578177799483166720", "created_at": "2026-11-10T17:30:56.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2120207593704767602"], "id": "2120207593704767602", "in_reply_to_user_id": "1745106082790318080", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 1, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2120025695283785966", "type": "replied_to"}], "text": "@SemiAnalysis_ Keeping 2048 pins while doubling per-pin speed shifts the hard problems to signal integrity on the interposer and the base-die PHY. It also means more I/O power packed into the same footprint, so thermal headroom on the stack gets tighter. Early field reliability data on HBM4E", "url": "https://x.com/MayaGPU/status/2120207593704767602"}, {"author_id": "2048022846564433920", "created_at": "2026-11-10T17:28:43.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2120207033886458227"], "id": "2120207033886458227", "in_reply_to_user_id": "1745106082790318080", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 30, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2120025695283785966", "type": "replied_to"}], "text": "@SemiAnalysis_ When will it come to market?", "url": "https://x.com/prmartinow/status/2120207033886458227"}, {"author_id": "2020406992410648576", "created_at": "2026-11-10T15:06:53.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2120171342905381041"], "id": "2120171342905381041", "in_reply_to_user_id": "1745106082790318080", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 63, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2120025695283785966", "type": "replied_to"}], "text": "@SemiAnalysis_ Good breakdown. The constraint has clearly moved from pin count to per-pin signal rate plus the backend interconnect — DRAM banks, TSV and the base-die PHY all have to scale together. That keeps value in advanced packaging and the base die, not just the DRAM stack. On the China", "url": "https://x.com/XiaoVic74463/status/2120171342905381041"}, {"author_id": "2077354681093718016", "created_at": "2026-11-10T14:50:10.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2120167136391795063"], "id": "2120167136391795063", "in_reply_to_user_id": "1745106082790318080", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 1, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2120025695283785966", "type": "replied_to"}], "text": "@SemiAnalysis_ Doubling pin speed at the same 2048 pins is the cleaner path, since widening the interface again would push interposer and routing costs up hard. The open question is signal integrity and power per bit at 28+ Gbps, which is where base die and packaging choices start to matter", "url": "https://x.com/Temperatur2com/status/2120167136391795063"}, {"author_id": "2050602410264190976", "created_at": "2026-11-10T14:29:35.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2120161954534932874"], "id": "2120161954534932874", "in_reply_to_user_id": "1745106082790318080", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 2, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2120025695283785966", "type": "replied_to"}], "text": "@SemiAnalysis_ Bandwidth is the bottleneck now, not compute. HBM5 doubling speed per pin without adding pins is exactly why memory buyers are locking in supply years ahead.\n\nhttps://t.co/FZ6n3Is1cR", "url": "https://x.com/ThematicInsight/status/2120161954534932874"}, {"author_id": "34567164", "created_at": "2026-11-10T12:41:03.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2120134640493060204"], "id": "2120134640493060204", "in_reply_to_user_id": "1745106082790318080", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 2, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2120025695283785966", "type": "replied_to"}], "text": "@SemiAnalysis_ HBM5 keeps HBM4E's 2048 pins and lifts pin speed from 14 Gbps to over 28 Gbps (Samsung, Hot Chips 2026). DRAM banks, TSVs, and the base-die PHY scale with that rate, and Samsung moves the PHY to the die edge, shortening the path to the GPU from ~5.5mm to ~2mm. The catch is", "url": "https://x.com/redboynono/status/2120134640493060204"}, {"author_id": "1661186814898733056", "created_at": "2026-11-10T11:42:18.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2120119857719259226"], "id": "2120119857719259226", "in_reply_to_user_id": "1745106082790318080", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 190, "like_count": 1, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2120025695283785966", "type": "replied_to"}], "text": "@SemiAnalysis_ Good threads.\n\nDesired speed is around 34 Gbps.", "url": "https://x.com/hcs_san/status/2120119857719259226"}, {"author_id": "1413079441937420288", "created_at": "2026-11-10T11:06:14.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2120110778649059592"], "id": "2120110778649059592", "in_reply_to_user_id": "1745106082790318080", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 1, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2120025695283785966", "type": "replied_to"}], "text": "@SemiAnalysis_ HBM is a big reason Micron sits #4 on my Elite Shortlist. Memory bandwidth is a real AI bottleneck, and AI infrastructure is still #1 on my sector board. \n\nStill waiting for an entry. starting to look better.... https://t.co/DmbfCYzVTw", "url": "https://x.com/FollowTheTides/status/2120110778649059592"}, {"author_id": "1719898634710614016", "created_at": "2026-11-10T10:32:11.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2120102213444042834"], "id": "2120102213444042834", "in_reply_to_user_id": "1745106082790318080", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 5, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2120025695283785966", "type": "replied_to"}], "text": "@SemiAnalysis_ Yo someone are spreading this, please confirm https://t.co/fIY6ha68Vb", "url": "https://x.com/TfLoooooo/status/2120102213444042834"}, {"author_id": "2064944226421637120", "created_at": "2026-11-10T10:21:05.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2120099416791035944"], "id": "2120099416791035944", "in_reply_to_user_id": "1745106082790318080", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 91, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2120025695283785966", "type": "replied_to"}], "text": "@SemiAnalysis_ Doubling bandwidth on the same 2,048 pins is the clean part. The later post in this thread is the constraint: the HBM5 PHY can run at more than 4× the power of HBM4E, which is why they added the thermal chimney.", "url": "https://x.com/Bluezbw/status/2120099416791035944"}, {"author_id": "2892119232", "created_at": "2026-11-10T08:43:34.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2120074879194267668"], "id": "2120074879194267668", "in_reply_to_user_id": "1745106082790318080", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 7, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2120025695283785966", "type": "replied_to"}], "text": "@SemiAnalysis_ For inference this is the spec that matters most: token generation is usually memory-bandwidth bound, not compute bound, so 2x bandwidth per stack can lift tokens/s more than a FLOPs bump. Curious how much of that 2x survives at the same power budget.", "url": "https://x.com/theVishalGhule/status/2120074879194267668"}, {"author_id": "2119243599170732032", "created_at": "2026-11-10T07:02:15.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2120049379520196984"], "id": "2120049379520196984", "in_reply_to_user_id": "1745106082790318080", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 0, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2120025697561317573", "type": "replied_to"}], "text": "@SemiAnalysis_ https://t.co/nDmwyB4QF9", "url": "https://x.com/Hannahlphi/status/2120049379520196984"}, {"author_id": "2119243599170732032", "created_at": "2026-11-10T07:02:00.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2120049319277375543"], "id": "2120049319277375543", "in_reply_to_user_id": "1745106082790318080", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 20, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2120025695283785966", "type": "replied_to"}], "text": "@SemiAnalysis_ https://t.co/nDmwyB4QF9", "url": "https://x.com/Hannahlphi/status/2120049319277375543"}], "includes": {"users": [{"id": "1968598802237136896", "name": "NeoWake", "public_metrics": {"followers_count": 1000, "following_count": 1540, "like_count": 2566, "listed_count": 0, "media_count": 23, "tweet_count": 1331}, "username": "Neo_Wake123"}, {"id": "961995849499795456", "name": "Anurag Bansal", "public_metrics": {"followers_count": 474, "following_count": 91, "like_count": 54, "listed_count": 19, "media_count": 321, "tweet_count": 1449}, "username": "boundlessanurag"}, {"id": "1578177799483166720", "name": "七小服 Seven Small Services", "public_metrics": {"followers_count": 58, "following_count": 657, "like_count": 316, "listed_count": 0, "media_count": 618, "tweet_count": 987}, "username": "MayaGPU"}, {"id": "2048022846564433920", "name": "Pierre Martinow", "public_metrics": {"followers_count": 27, "following_count": 479, "like_count": 1179, "listed_count": 1, "media_count": 25, "tweet_count": 353}, "username": "prmartinow"}, {"id": "2020406992410648576", "name": "ViiiC", "public_metrics": {"followers_count": 2, "following_count": 17, "like_count": 5, "listed_count": 0, "media_count": 0, "tweet_count": 23}, "username": "XiaoVic74463"}, {"id": "2077354681093718016", "name": "Temperature2.com", "public_metrics": {"followers_count": 43, "following_count": 410, "like_count": 286, "listed_count": 0, "media_count": 337, "tweet_count": 1755}, "username": "Temperatur2com"}, {"id": "2050602410264190976", "name": "Thematic Insights", "public_metrics": {"followers_count": 3, "following_count": 53, "like_count": 12, "listed_count": 0, "media_count": 46, "tweet_count": 482}, "username": "ThematicInsight"}, {"id": "34567164", "name": "Steven.Sun", "public_metrics": {"followers_count": 191, "following_count": 203, "like_count": 353, "listed_count": 4, "media_count": 29, "tweet_count": 3381}, "username": "redboynono"}, {"id": "1661186814898733056", "name": "San | ⚡", "public_metrics": {"followers_count": 598, "following_count": 599, "like_count": 2665, "listed_count": 7, "media_count": 290, "tweet_count": 2782}, "username": "hcs_san"}, {"id": "1413079441937420288", "name": "Christian", "public_metrics": {"followers_count": 12, "following_count": 69, "like_count": 113, "listed_count": 0, "media_count": 54, "tweet_count": 144}, "username": "FollowTheTides"}, {"id": "1719898634710614016", "name": "Sir Bagsalot", "public_metrics": {"followers_count": 60, "following_count": 1157, "like_count": 479, "listed_count": 0, "media_count": 8, "tweet_count": 189}, "username": "TfLoooooo"}, {"id": "2064944226421637120", "name": "Blue", "public_metrics": {"followers_count": 1962, "following_count": 1844, "like_count": 1571, "listed_count": 1, "media_count": 22, "tweet_count": 2574}, "username": "Bluezbw"}, {"id": "2892119232", "name": "Vishal Ghule", "public_metrics": {"followers_count": 45, "following_count": 154, "like_count": 27, "listed_count": 0, "media_count": 16, "tweet_count": 100}, "username": "theVishalGhule"}, {"id": "2119243599170732032", "name": "Hannah", "public_metrics": {"followers_count": 1, "following_count": 229, "like_count": 40, "listed_count": 0, "media_count": 0, "tweet_count": 337}, "username": "Hannahlphi"}]}, "meta": {"newest_id": "2120287263481626981", "next_token": "b26v89c19zqg8o3juzovbxukowovzbhb5ay1wj4ijko71", "oldest_id": "2120049319277375543", "result_count": 15}}